window.ABCM_DOCS = [{"t":"Quick start","u":"guides/quick-start.html","d":"Install the extension, tick a few chats, export a list and delete or archive them. About five minutes.","h":["1. Install the extension","2. Open a chat site","3. Start selecting","4. Tick some chats","5. Export a list first (optional)","6. Delete or archive","7. Finish","What to try next"],"x":"What you will do: install the extension, start selecting on a chat site, tick a few chats, save a list of them, and then delete or archive them. Before you start: you need a desktop browser (Chrome, Edge or Firefox 140 or newer) and an account on at least one of ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini or Grok. Sign in to it first. You do not need to change any settings. 1. Install the extension # Add it from the Chrome Web Store . On Edge and Firefox the steps differ a little, so follow Installation . Then pin the toolbar icon so it is always in reach. Click the Extensions (puzzle piece) button in the toolbar, find AI Bulk Chat Manager and click its pin. 2. Open a chat site # Go to chatgpt.com , claude.ai , gemini.google.com or grok.com . Make sure the chat list is showing in the sidebar. If the sidebar is closed, open it. Tab already open? If the site was open before you installed the extension, you do not need to reload it. Clicking the toolbar icon attaches the extension to that tab. If the popup says Can't reach the site, click Reload page . 3. Start selecting # Click the toolbar icon, then click Start selecting chats . Or press Alt + Shift + B . You should see: a checkbox next to every chat in the sidebar, and a small panel in the bottom corner of the page. The panel is titled AI Bulk Chat Manager , shows the site name, and reads 0 selected with a line such as of 20 chats shown . 4. Tick some chats # Click chats in the sidebar. Clicking a row ticks it. It does not open the chat while you are selecting. The count in the panel goes up as you tick. Click Select all to tick every chat that is shown. Hold Shift and click a second chat to tick everything between it and the last one you ticked. Click Clear to start again. Five chats ticked. The buttons at the bottom of the panel act on exactly these chats. The full list of ways to select is in Selecting chats . 5. Export a list first (optional) # Click Export and choose JSON , CSV or Markdown . Your browser saves a file with the titles and links of the selected chats. A message such as Exported 5 chats as JSON appears in the panel. Nothing is deleted. See Exporting . 6. Delete or archive # Press the button Click Delete . When chats are selected the button shows the count, for example Delete 5 . On ChatGPT you can click Archive instead. The other three sites have no archive, so the button is hidden there. Check the list A dialog asks Delete 5 chats? and lists every chat. The Cancel button has the focus. Read the list. If it is wrong, press Cancel or Esc . Confirm Click Delete 5 chats . The panel shows Deleting chats&hellip; , a progress bar and a Stop button. Read the result The panel shows a summary such as 5 chats deleted . Click Done to go back to selecting. Deleting cannot be undone A deleted chat is gone from the site. The extension has no recycle bin and cannot bring it back. Use Export first if you may want the titles later. On ChatGPT, Archive can be reversed from ChatGPT's own settings. 7. Finish # Click the X in the panel (its tooltip is Finish and close ), or press Alt + Shift + B again. The checkboxes disappear and your selection is forgotten. You can also click Finish selecting in the toolbar popup. What to try next # Load all older chats so that Select all reaches your whole history. Understand fast mode and what to do when a chat fails. Change the settings , such as the extra confirmation threshold. Read the limits before you delete a lot of chats."},{"t":"Installation","u":"guides/installation.html","d":"Install AI Bulk Chat Manager on Chrome, Edge or Firefox, or load it from source. Includes the first-run tip for tabs that were already open.","h":["Chrome and other Chromium browsers","Microsoft Edge","Firefox","From source","First run: tabs that were already open","Check that it works","Updating and removing"],"x":"Works on: desktop Chrome and other Chromium browsers (Chrome 111 or newer), Microsoft Edge, and Firefox 140 or newer. Chrome and Edge use the same package. Works with: ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini and Grok, on these addresses only: chatgpt.com , chat.openai.com , claude.ai , gemini.google.com and grok.com . Chrome and other Chromium browsers # Open the Chrome Web Store page . Click Add to Chrome and confirm. Click the Extensions (puzzle piece) button in the toolbar and pin AI Bulk Chat Manager . Brave, Opera, Vivaldi and other Chromium browsers that install Chrome extensions use the same page. Microsoft Edge # Edge can install extensions from the Chrome Web Store. Open the Chrome Web Store page in Edge. If Edge shows a banner, choose Allow extensions from other stores . Click Add to Chrome and confirm. Or load the Chrome package from the latest release : unzip ai-bulk-chat-manager-<version>.zip , open edge://extensions , turn on Developer mode , click Load unpacked and choose the unzipped folder. Firefox # Firefox needs version 140 or newer, on desktop. Until the extension is listed on Firefox Add-ons, load the release package as a temporary add-on. Download ai-bulk-chat-manager-<version>-firefox.zip from the latest release . Type about:debugging in the address bar and open This Firefox . Click Load Temporary Add-on and choose the zip file. Temporary means temporary Firefox removes a temporary add-on when you close the browser, so you repeat these steps next time. A listing on Firefox Add-ons would not have this limit. Firefox asks for access to the five chat sites when you add the extension. That access is what lets it add checkboxes to the chat list. See Privacy and permissions . If you decline it, the extension cannot work on those sites. From source # You can run the extension straight from the source code. Download or clone the repository . Open chrome://extensions (or edge://extensions ) and turn on Developer mode . Click Load unpacked and choose the extension folder. For Firefox, build the Firefox package first, because Firefox needs a slightly different manifest. With Node.js installed, run this in the repository folder, then load dist/ai-bulk-chat-manager-<version>-firefox.zip as shown above. node scripts/build.mjs --firefox A copy loaded from source has a different extension identity from the store version. Both can be installed side by side. First run: tabs that were already open # Browsers add an extension to a page only when the page loads after the install. A chat tab that was open before you installed has no extension in it yet. You do not need to reload. Open that tab and click the toolbar icon (or press Alt + Shift + B ). The extension attaches itself to the tab and starts. If it cannot, the popup says Can't reach the site and offers Reload page . Check that it works # Open one of the chat sites and sign in. Click the toolbar icon. The status card should say Ready on followed by the site name. Click Start selecting chats . Checkboxes appear in the sidebar and the panel opens. If something differs, see Troubleshooting . Updating and removing # Store versions update through your browser, which checks for new versions by itself. A copy loaded from source or as a temporary add-on does not update itself. Load the newer files again. To remove it, use your browser's extensions page. Removing the extension also removes the settings it stored. Files you exported stay in your downloads folder until you delete them."},{"t":"Selecting chats","u":"guides/selecting-chats.html","d":"Start selecting, tick chats with clicks, Shift-click ranges, Select all, Invert, title filter, Oldest N, and Load all older chats.","h":["Start and finish selecting","The panel","Tick chats with clicks","Select a range with Shift-click","Select all, Clear and Invert","Select by title or position","Load all older chats","Checkboxes while you scroll","Selection tips"],"x":"Selecting happens in two places: the checkboxes in the site's sidebar, and the panel. This page covers both. Start and finish selecting # Selecting is off until you turn it on. Nothing changes on the site before that. You have three ways to start: Click the toolbar icon, then Start selecting chats . Press Alt + Shift + B on a supported site. Click the optional launcher button, if you turned it on in the settings . When selecting starts, each chat in the sidebar gets a checkbox and the panel opens. To stop, click X in the panel ( Finish and close ), press the shortcut again, or click Finish selecting in the popup. Finishing removes every checkbox and forgets the selection. Keep the chat list visible The extension only sees chats that the page shows. If the sidebar is closed, the panel says No chats found yet. Open the chat list in the sidebar or scroll it, and they will appear here. Open the sidebar and the chats appear. The panel # The panel floats over the page. It shows the site name, a big count of selected chats, and a line such as of 20 chats shown . That second number counts the chats that are currently in the page and not hidden. Drag the panel by its title bar. It remembers where you left it. Minimize shrinks it to the title bar and the count. The button then changes to Expand . Panel settings (the sliders icon) opens a small box with the Add checkboxes as you scroll and Fast mode switches and an All settings link to the Options page. Finish and close (the X) ends selecting. Tick chats with clicks # Click the checkbox of a chat, or click anywhere on its row. Both tick it. Rows do not open while you select While selecting, a click on a chat row ticks it instead of opening the chat. This is on purpose, so you cannot open a chat by accident. The site's own buttons inside the row, such as its three-dot menu, still work. Click Finish selecting to get normal clicking back. A ticked chat is highlighted. The selection survives when the site redraws its list. Select a range with Shift-click # Tick one chat. Hold Shift and click another chat, either its checkbox or its row. Every chat shown between the two is ticked. Shift-click only ticks. It does not untick a range. Select all, Clear and Invert # Select all Ticks every chat that is shown. Clear Unticks everything. Invert Ticks the chats that are not ticked and unticks the ones that are, among the chats shown. Select all and Invert work on the chats currently in the page. A long history is not all in the page. See Load all older chats below. Select by title or position # Click Select by title or position to open two extra tools. By title Type part of a title in Part of a chat title , then click Select (or press Enter ). Every shown chat whose title contains that text is ticked. Capital letters do not matter. The text is also compared with the chat's link. Click Unselect to untick the matching chats instead. A message such as 3 chats matched tells you how many were found. By position: Oldest Type a number in the Oldest box (1 to 500, default 10), then click Select or Unselect . The extension takes the last N chats in the list. The sites list newest chats first, so those are the oldest ones. Load first, then pick the oldest Oldest counts from the bottom of the chats that are in the page right now. If your history is not fully loaded, the bottom of the page is not your oldest chat. Click Load all older chats first. Load all older chats # The sites load a chat list in pages as you scroll. Most of a long history is not in the page until you scroll down to it. Load all older chats does the scrolling for you. Click Load all older chats in the panel. The button shows progress, for example Loading chats&hellip; 140 (click to stop) . The sidebar scrolls to the bottom again and again until nothing new arrives. When it ends, a message such as 320 chats in the list appears. The sidebar goes back to where it was, and every loaded chat has a checkbox. Click the button again at any time to stop. It scrolls only the chat list, never a conversation. The button is disabled until at least one chat is shown. Checkboxes while you scroll # With Add checkboxes as you scroll on (the default), chats that the site loads while you scroll get checkboxes automatically. The extension also notices when the site replaces the whole sidebar. Turn the switch off in the panel settings, the popup or the Options page if you prefer to add checkboxes only when you start. Selection tips # The count in the panel is the truth. Look at it before you press Delete . Chats inside collapsed or hidden parts of the sidebar are not \"shown\". Select all skips them. Only real clicks count. Clicks that a script on the site sends are ignored, so a page cannot build a selection for you. Selection lives in the page. Reloading the tab loses it."},{"t":"Deleting and archiving","u":"guides/deleting-and-archiving.html","d":"The confirmation dialog, fast mode and page menus, progress, Stop, results, Retry failed and Copy report.","h":["Delete or archive","The confirmation dialog","How the work is done","Progress and Stop","The result","Before you delete a lot"],"x":"Deleting cannot be undone The extension asks the site to delete your chats. Once a site has deleted a chat, neither you nor this extension can bring it back. If you might want the titles and links later, export them first . On ChatGPT, Archive is reversible. Delete or archive # Both actions work on the chats you ticked. Press the button at the bottom of the panel. Delete Available on ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini and Grok. With chats selected the button shows the count, for example Delete 5 . Archive Available on ChatGPT only. The chats leave your chat list and you can restore them from ChatGPT's archive. The other three sites do not offer archiving, so the Archive button is hidden there. Both buttons are disabled until you tick at least one chat. The confirmation dialog # Nothing happens until you confirm. A dialog opens over the page. The dialog names the site, lists each chat and puts focus on Cancel. The title asks Delete 5 chats? (or Archive 5 chats? ). The text under it says where the chats will be removed from. For a delete it adds This can't be undone. The list shows the title of every selected chat. With more than eight chats a search box appears, labelled Search the selected chats , to find a title in the list. Cancel has the focus when the dialog opens, not the destructive button. Pressing Enter at once cancels. Esc closes the dialog. So does a click outside it. Tab stays inside the dialog. The extra tick for big deletes When you delete more chats than a threshold, the dialog also shows I understand this can't be undone. The red button stays disabled until you tick it. The default threshold is 20, so deleting 21 or more needs the tick. Change it in Options, Behavior , in Extra confirmation above (1 to 500). Archiving never needs the tick. How the work is done # There are two routes. The extension picks one for each chat. Fast mode (the default) On ChatGPT, Claude and Grok, fast mode asks the site directly to delete or archive each chat. It sends the same kind of request the site's own buttons send, from the page you are on, using the session you are already signed in with. A few chats are handled at a time with short pauses between requests, and the chat disappears from the sidebar when it is done. This is much faster and does not need the site's menus on screen. If the site asks the extension to slow down, it waits and tries that chat once more. Page menus (the fallback) The extension clicks through the site's own menus like a person: it opens the chat's three-dot menu, chooses Delete (or Archive ) and confirms in the site's dialog. It does this one chat at a time, so it is slower. It is used when: you turned Fast mode off; the site is Gemini, which has no request the extension can use, so Gemini always uses its menus (the Fast mode switch is disabled there); a fast request failed for a chat: the site refused it, the network failed, the session was rejected, or the site changed the way the request works. Only the chats that failed fast go through the menus. The rest are not repeated. How it avoids clicking the wrong thing It looks for the three-dot button inside that chat's own row, never elsewhere in the sidebar. It picks a menu item by its label, never by its position. It knows the words for Delete and Archive in more than two dozen interface languages. An item such as Remove from project is never chosen for Delete. The confirm button in the site's dialog must also match. If the dialog only offers Cancel or unknown buttons, it clicks nothing and reports a failure. After a page-menu delete it checks that the chat really left the list. If it is still there, the chat counts as failed. Only real clicks and keys from you drive the panel. A script on the site cannot press Delete for you. Progress and Stop # Progress while a run is under way. While it works, the panel shows Deleting chats&hellip; (or Archiving chats&hellip; ), a count such as 4 of 6 , a progress bar, the title of the chat in progress and, if any failed, a line like 1 failed . Click Stop to end the run early. The request already in flight finishes. No more are started. The result says Stopped after 3 of 6 and Chats you didn't get to are still selected. While a run is going: Keep the tab open, and keep it in front. The work happens inside the page. Do not change the chat list yourself. Unticking a chat skips it. It is then listed as failed with the reason You unticked it during the run. You cannot close the panel until the run ends. Click Stop first. The result # When a chat fails, it stays selected and its reason is listed. The summary title is one of these: Title Meaning 5 chats deleted or 5 chats archived Everything worked. The chats are gone from the list and deselected. 5 of 6 done, 1 failed Some worked. The failed ones are listed with a reason and stay selected. Nothing was changed. 3 chats failed. Every chat failed. Nothing was deleted or archived. Stopped after 3 of 6 You pressed Stop . The rest are still selected. Retry failed and Copy report Retry failed goes back to selecting and opens the confirmation again for the chats that are still selected, which includes the failed ones. Confirm to try again. Copy report copies one line per failed chat (its title and the reason) to your clipboard and shows Report copied . The report contains chat titles, so read it before you paste it somewhere public. Done goes back to selecting. Failure reasons and what to try Reason shown What it means and what to try The chat is no longer in the list. The site removed or redrew the row. Reload the page, start selecting again and retry. The chat is hidden in the sidebar. The row was collapsed or filtered out. Show it, then retry. Couldn't read the chat's id. The site changed its links. Update the extension and report it if it persists. You unticked it during the run. Not an error. You removed it from the selection. The page changed while working. The site redrew the list during the run. Retry. The site asked to slow down (rate limit). Wait a minute, then retry a smaller batch. The site rejected the session. Reload the page and sign in again. Your sign-in expired. Reload, sign in, retry. Network error. Check your connection and retry. The site refused the request (404). The site refused it. The number is the HTTP code. The chat may already be gone, or the site changed. Try turning Fast mode off. Couldn't find your Claude organization. Reload claude.ai, make sure you are signed in, retry. This site can't archive chats. Archive exists on ChatGPT only. Use Delete or Export . Couldn't find the chat's menu button. The chat's menu didn't open. Couldn't find the menu item. Couldn't find the confirmation button. The confirmation didn't complete. The page-menu route could not follow the site's page. The site may have changed. Retry once. If it keeps failing, see Limits and report it . The chat was still in the list after deleting. The site did not remove the chat. Reload the page to see the real state, then retry. The action didn't complete. Something went wrong (code). Retry. If it repeats, report it with the text shown. Before you delete a lot # Click Load all older chats if you want to reach your whole history. Tick a small batch first, for example 10 chats, to see how the site behaves. Export the list if you may need the titles later. Read the list in the confirmation dialog, not just the count."},{"t":"Exporting a list of chats","u":"guides/exporting.html","d":"Save the titles and links of the selected chats as JSON, CSV or Markdown. What the file contains and where it goes.","h":["Export step by step","What is in the file","The three formats","File name and location","Tips"],"x":"What it does: creates a file from the chats you ticked and saves it to your computer. It changes nothing on the site. Export step by step # Tick the chats Select the chats you want in the list. Export is disabled until at least one chat is ticked. It works on all four sites. Open the Export menu Click Export in the panel. A small menu opens with three choices. Choose a format Click JSON , CSV or Markdown . Your browser saves the file and the panel shows a message such as Exported 5 chats as Markdown . The Export menu has three formats. Press Esc to close the menu without exporting. What is in the file # Each exported chat has three things: its title , its full link (starting with https:// ) and its id . The file also records the site name and the time of the export. The file never contains your conversation text. The extension does not read conversations, only the chat list that the sidebar shows. Titles can be private A chat title can reveal a lot. Read the file before you share it or attach it to a bug report. The three formats # Format Use it for What it looks like JSON Scripts and other programs. An object with exportedAt , site , count and a chats list. Each chat has title , url and id . CSV Spreadsheets such as Excel. A header line title,url,id , then one line per chat. The file starts with a byte order mark so Excel reads non-Latin titles correctly. A title that begins with = , + , - or @ gets a leading apostrophe so a spreadsheet does not run it as a formula. Markdown Notes apps and readable lists. A heading with the site name and the count, then one bullet per chat as a link: - [Title](link) . File name and location # Files are named ai-chats-<site>-<date and time>.<format> , for example ai-chats-chatgpt-2026-10-08T12-30-00.json . Your browser decides where the file goes. By default that is your downloads folder. If you set your browser to ask where to save each file, it asks. The file is made on your device and is not uploaded anywhere. Tips # Export before a big delete. The file is a record of titles and links, not a backup of the conversations. After you delete a chat, its link stops working. Use Load all older chats first if you want your whole history in the file."},{"t":"The toolbar popup","u":"guides/popup-and-footer.html","d":"The status card, the two switches, the rotating About, GitHub, Rate and Support footer, and the monthly support note.","h":["The status card","The header","The two switches","The rotating footer","The monthly support note"],"x":"The popup is a small control center. It does not hold the selection tools. Those are in the panel inside the chat page. The popup starts and ends selecting, and holds two quick switches. The popup while selecting is on. The status card # The card at the top tells you what the extension sees on the current tab. The card says What it means What to do Checking this page&hellip; It is looking at the tab. Wait a moment. Ready on ChatGPT and Start selecting to put a checkbox next to each chat. A supported site, not selecting yet. Click Start selecting chats . Selecting on ChatGPT and 2 chats selected Selecting is on in this tab. Click Finish selecting to end it. Can't reach ChatGPT yet and Reload the page, then try again. The extension could not attach to this tab. Click Reload page . This page isn't supported and Works on ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini and Grok. You are on some other page. Click one of the four site buttons shown to open that site in a new tab. Then click the icon again. The site name in the card is the real site (ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini or Grok). When you click the main button, the popup closes so it does not get in the way of the page. Under the button, Shortcut: shows the current keyboard shortcut if one is set. See Keyboard and shortcuts . The header # The header shows the name and the version, for example v9.0.0 . The sliders button ( Settings ) opens the Options page in a new tab. The two switches # Fast mode Ask the site directly first, then fall back to its menus. The same setting as in the Options page. See How the work is done . Add checkboxes as you scroll Newly loaded chats get a checkbox automatically. The same setting as in the Options page. Both save at once. Changes also show in the open panel. The rotating footer # At the bottom of the popup, a short message and a button rotate through four items. The four tabs under them are About , GitHub , Rate and Support . Tab Message Button About Copyright (c) 2026 Ehsan Enaloo. Released under the MIT License. Learn More opens the developer's website, www.enaloo.com. The About section of the Options page also links to it. GitHub Source code, releases, and project details. Open GitHub opens the repository. Rate Enjoying the extension? A good rating helps the extension build trust faster. Rate on Store opens the review page for your browser's store. Support Saving you time? Support the project with a small coffee. Buy Me a Coffee opens the donation page. The footer moves to the next item every five seconds. A thin line under the tabs shows the time left. It pauses while the pointer is over it or a footer control has the keyboard focus. Click a tab to show that item and restart the timer. If your system asks for reduced motion, the footer stays on the first item and does not rotate. The buttons open web pages in a new tab only when you click them. The monthly support note # The extension is free and has no ads. About two weeks after you install it, and then at most once every 30 days, it does two things: A small heart appears on the toolbar icon. The next time you open the popup, a note titled Free and ad-free appears. It reads: If this saves you time, a small coffee helps keep it updated. Shown at most once a month. The note has these choices: Buy me a coffee opens the donation page. Rate opens the store review page. Not now hides the note until the next reminder. Don't show again turns the reminder off for good, including the heart. Nothing is sent when the note appears. The only thing stored is a small timer on your device. See Privacy and permissions ."},{"t":"Settings reference","u":"guides/settings-reference.html","d":"Every option with its default: language, theme, accent, fast mode, checkboxes as you scroll, confirmation threshold, launcher, shortcut, reset and diagnostics.","h":["Open the Options page","Appearance","Behavior","Keyboard shortcut","Privacy","About","Remembered automatically"],"x":"Settings live on the Options page. They save the moment you change them and apply to the popup, the panel and every open chat tab. Open the Options page # Click the toolbar icon, then the sliders button ( Settings ) in the popup header. Or open the panel's Panel settings box and click All settings . Or use the Options link of the extension on your browser's extensions page. The Options page. The left list jumps to each section. Appearance # Setting Choices Default Language Automatic (browser language) or one of 11 languages. The language of this extension's screens. See Languages and appearance . Automatic Theme System , Light , Dark System Accent color Teal , Blue , Indigo , Graphite Teal Behavior # Setting What it does Default Fast mode Deletes and archives through the site's own request, which is much faster and does not need its menus on screen. If a request fails, the extension falls back to clicking through the page's menus, one chat at a time. Turn it off to always use the menus. Has no effect on Gemini, which always uses its menus. On Add checkboxes as you scroll While you are selecting, chats that the site loads as you scroll get checkboxes automatically. On Extra confirmation above When you delete more chats than this number, you must also tick a box in the confirmation dialog. Accepts 1 to 500. A number outside that range is brought back into it. 20 Show a launcher button on chat pages A small button in the corner of ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini and Grok that opens the panel. Off The two switches Fast mode and Add checkboxes as you scroll are also in the popup and in the panel's Panel settings box. They are the same settings. The launcher button With the launcher on, a small round button with the extension's logo sits in the corner of the supported chat pages. Click it to start selecting without using the toolbar. It shows when the panel is closed and hides while the panel is open. Its tooltip reads Open AI Bulk Chat Manager . Keyboard shortcut # Shows the current key for Open or close the panel , or Not set . The button Change shortcut opens your browser's own shortcut settings page. If your browser blocks that, the extension tells you where to go. The default is Alt + Shift + B . See Keyboard and shortcuts . Privacy # This section lists the main privacy facts and has three buttons. Privacy policy Opens the policy. Copy diagnostics Copies a short text for bug reports and shows Diagnostics copied. Paste them into a bug report. It holds the extension version, your browser name and its user-agent text, the interface language, your settings, and a note that it contains no chat titles or links. See Reporting a problem . Reset settings Asks Reset all settings to their defaults? After you confirm, every setting above returns to its default, including where you dragged the panel, and you see Settings were reset. It does not touch your chats or the monthly support reminder timer. About # The About section has a short description, the independence notice and these buttons: Guide (this site), Source (GitHub), Report a problem (the issue forms), Rate , Support and Website . Website and the byline under the buttons link to the developer's website, www.enaloo.com . All of them open in a new tab only when you click them. Remembered automatically # Two more things are remembered without a setting you can see: Where you last dragged the panel. The timer for the monthly support note , and whether you chose Don't show again . Settings are stored in your browser on this device, not in browser sync. They do not follow you to another computer. See Privacy and permissions ."},{"t":"Languages and appearance","u":"guides/languages-and-appearance.html","d":"The 11 interface languages, right-to-left layouts, light and dark themes and the four accent colors.","h":["Language","Right-to-left layouts","Theme","Accent color","This guide's own theme"],"x":"Language # The extension's screens (popup, panel, confirmation, results and Options page) come in 11 languages. Change it in Options, Appearance, Language . Language Shown in the list as Direction English English Left to right Persian فارسی Right to left Spanish Español Left to right French Français Left to right German Deutsch Left to right Brazilian Portuguese Português (Brasil) Left to right Russian Русский Left to right Simplified Chinese 简体中文 Left to right Japanese 日本語 Left to right Arabic العربية Right to left Hindi हिन्दी Left to right The default is Automatic (browser language) . The extension follows your browser's language. If it does not have that language, it uses English. Chinese maps to Simplified Chinese and Portuguese to Brazilian Portuguese. When you pick a language, an open panel switches at once. Any text that is missing in a language shows in English, never blank. This is the language of the extension only. It does not change the language of ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini or Grok. Found a wrong or awkward translation? Use the translation fix form . Right-to-left layouts # With Persian or Arabic, the panel, popup and Options page switch to right-to-left. The panel and its buttons flip so that the start of a line is on the right. Checkboxes sit at the start edge of each chat row, so on a site that is shown in a right-to-left language they appear on the right. The panel in Persian. Everything is mirrored, including the order of the buttons. The popup in Persian. The confirmation in Persian. Theme # In Options, Appearance, Theme choose: System Follows your operating system or browser. This is the default. Light Always light. Dark Always dark. The setting applies to the panel, the popup and the Options page. The panel switches as soon as you change it. With System , it also follows your system when that changes. The same panel in the dark theme. Accent color # The accent color tints buttons, switches and highlights in the extension. Choose it in Options, Appearance, Accent color . Teal (default) Blue Indigo Graphite (a neutral dark gray-blue) The color of the highlight on ticked chats in the site's sidebar stays teal for every accent. The red Delete button also stays red, so it always looks like a danger button. This guide's own theme # This website follows your system theme as well. The Dark mode or Light mode button in the header switches it, and your choice is remembered in this browser. That choice is separate from the extension's theme."},{"t":"Keyboard and shortcuts","u":"guides/keyboard-and-shortcuts.html","d":"The Alt+Shift+B shortcut, how to change it, and the keys that work inside the panel and the confirmation dialog.","h":["The global shortcut","Change the shortcut","Inside the panel","Inside the confirmation dialog","In the toolbar popup","On this guide site"],"x":"The global shortcut # The extension has one shortcut, set up through your browser. Action Default key Open or close the panel (start or finish selecting) Alt + Shift + B It works on ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini and Grok. On any other page it does nothing. It works in a tab that was open before you installed the extension. The extension attaches itself to the tab first. While a run is going, pressing it to finish does not close the panel. The panel tells you to Stop the running action first. On a Mac, Alt is the Option key. Change the shortcut # Open the Options page and go to Keyboard shortcut . Click Change shortcut . Your browser's shortcut page opens: chrome://extensions/shortcuts in Chrome, edge://extensions/shortcuts in Edge, and the Add-ons manager in Firefox ( about:addons ). Find Open or close the selection panel under AI Bulk Chat Manager and set your key. If the Options page shows Not set , the default key was probably taken by another extension or by the browser. Set a key in the same place. Some browsers block a link to their own pages. If that happens, the Options page tells you where to go by hand. Inside the panel # Key What it does Tab and Shift + Tab Move between the panel's buttons and boxes. Enter or Space Press the focused button. Enter in Part of a chat title Runs Select for that text. Esc with the Export menu open Closes the menu and returns to Export . Shift + click on a chat Ticks every shown chat between it and the last one you ticked. Keys you type in the panel do not reach the site, so they do not trigger the site's own shortcuts. Inside the confirmation dialog # Key What it does Esc Closes the dialog without doing anything. Tab and Shift + Tab Move around inside the dialog. The focus does not leave it. Enter when it opens Presses Cancel , because Cancel has the focus. To confirm, move to the red button or click it. In the toolbar popup # The popup has no shortcuts of its own. Use Tab and Enter like on any page. It shows the current shortcut under the main button. On this guide site # Press / to jump to the search box."},{"t":"Privacy and permissions","u":"guides/privacy-and-permissions.html","d":"What the extension reads, stores and sends (nothing leaves your device), and why it needs each permission.","h":["The short version","What it reads","What it stores","What it sends","Permissions and why","Export files, reports and diagnostics","Third parties","Removing your data"],"x":"This page is the friendly version. The legal text is the privacy policy , which is the same as docs/PRIVACY.md in the repository. If the two ever differ, the policy wins. The short version # The extension has no server. It collects nothing about you and sends nothing to its author or to anyone else. No account, no sign-in, no analytics, no telemetry, no ads, no crash reports. It never reads the text of your conversations. It reads the chat list in the sidebar (titles and links), and only while you are selecting. Only two things are stored, in your browser: your settings and a small timer for the monthly support reminder. When you delete or archive, the request goes to the site you are on, using the session you are already signed in with, and nowhere else. It acts only on chatgpt.com , chat.openai.com , claude.ai , gemini.google.com and grok.com . What it reads # What Why Where it goes The chat list in the sidebar: each chat's title, link and id To add checkboxes, count your selection and tell the site which chats to delete or archive. Held in the page's memory while you select. Not saved, not sent. Forgotten when you finish selecting or close the page. The address and tab of the page you are on To know whether it is a supported site and to start the panel there. Used on your device. Not sent. Your settings To remember your choices. Your browser's local extension storage. The clipboard (write only) To copy a failure report or diagnostics when you click Copy report or Copy diagnostics . Written on your click. The extension never reads your clipboard. It does not read messages or conversation content, your account details, payment details or cookies. It does not read pages other than the five supported sites. Titles are shown as plain text and never run as page code. What it stores # Two small items in your browser's local extension storage, on this device. It does not use browser sync storage, so the extension itself does not copy them to your other devices. Your settings: language, theme, accent color, Fast mode, checkboxes as you scroll, the confirmation threshold, whether the launcher shows, and where you last dragged the panel. No chat titles, links or account details. The support-reminder timer: when you installed, when the note was last shown, how many times, and whether you chose Don't show again . It keeps no history of your chats, selections or deletions, and no export files or logs. What it sends # The extension makes no requests to its author or to any third party. Its translations and styles are packaged inside it. The only network requests it causes happen after you select chats and confirm Delete or Archive . They go from the chat page to the same site, with the session you are signed in with, the way the site's own buttons work. They contain no chat titles. The ones that change a chat contain only that chat's id and, for ChatGPT, a short \"hidden\" or \"archived\" flag. Site What happens in fast mode ChatGPT It asks the site for the short-lived access token that the site's own page uses (kept in memory for up to five minutes, never stored), then sends one request per chat to hide (delete) or archive it. Claude It asks the site for your organization id, then sends one delete request per chat. There is no archive. Grok It sends one delete request per chat. There is no archive. Gemini No request. It clicks through the page's own menu and dialog, as a person would. Those requests use the sites' own internal addresses, which are not public or documented and can change without notice. If you turn Fast mode off, or a request fails, the extension clicks through the site's menus instead and makes no extra request. What the sites do with these requests is up to them. For example, how long a site keeps a deleted or archived chat is the site's decision. Two more things use the network, but not on the extension's initiative: links you choose to click (the guide, GitHub, the privacy policy, the developer's website, the donation page and the store review page, which open in a new tab only when you click them), and your browser's own check for extension updates. Permissions and why # Permission Why it is needed storage Keeps your settings and the reminder timer on your device. activeTab Lets the extension work with the tab you are on when you click the toolbar icon or use the shortcut. scripting Loads the extension's own scripts into a chat tab that was open before the install, so you do not have to reload. Only the extension's packaged files are loaded. Access to the five chat sites Lets the extension add checkboxes to the chat list and send the delete or archive request on those sites. Your browser may word it as \"Read and change your data on\" those sites. The extension uses it only as described here. Firefox asks for the same five sites when you add the extension. The keyboard shortcut Not a permission. It opens or closes the panel. You can change it. The extension does not ask for your browsing history, bookmarks, downloads, cookies, list of tabs or access to any other website. Export files, reports and diagnostics # Export makes a file on your device with each chat's title, link and id. It is not uploaded. See Exporting . Copy report copies the titles of failed chats and the reasons. It contains titles, so read it before you paste it in public. Copy diagnostics copies the version, your browser, the language and your settings. It contains no chat titles, links or page content. The extension sends none of these anywhere. Third parties # There are none. No analytics, ads or crash reporting, and no remote code, fonts or images. This guide website also loads nothing from other sites: no fonts, scripts, trackers or analytics. Removing your data # Settings: Options, Privacy, Reset settings restores the defaults. Everything: uninstall the extension. The browser then deletes its storage. Chats you deleted or archived: those changes were made on the site and cannot be undone by the extension. Export files: they are in your downloads folder. Delete them yourself. The author holds no copy of anything, so there is nothing to request from the author."},{"t":"Privacy policy","u":"privacy.html","d":"The full privacy policy of AI Bulk Chat Manager: no server, no analytics, nothing sent to the author.","h":["Summary","How it works","What the extension can access","What is stored","What the extension sends over the network","Exporting","Copy report and Copy diagnostics","Permissions and why each is needed","Monthly support reminder","Third parties","Chrome Web Store Limited Use","Firefox","Removing your data","Children","Open source","Changes to this policy","Contact"],"x":"AI Bulk Chat Manager (the \"extension\") Last updated: 2026-10-08 AI Bulk Chat Manager is a browser extension for Chrome, Edge and Firefox. It lets you select many chats at once on ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini and Grok, and then delete, archive or export them. This policy explains what the extension reads, what it stores, and what leaves your device. The short version: the extension has no server, collects nothing about you, and sends no data to its author or to any third party. This page is the web version of docs/PRIVACY.md in the repository. For a friendlier explanation, read Privacy and permissions . Summary # The extension does not collect, transmit, sell or share personal data. There is no account, sign-in, analytics, telemetry, advertising or crash reporting. It never reads the text of your conversations. It only reads the chat list in each site's sidebar (the titles and links of your chats), and only while you are selecting chats. Only two things are stored, in your browser: your settings, and a small timer for the monthly support reminder. When you delete or archive chats, the extension asks the site you are on to do it. The request goes to that site, using the session you are already signed in with, and nowhere else. It works only on chatgpt.com , chat.openai.com , claude.ai , gemini.google.com and grok.com . How it works # The extension runs in your browser. A content script is loaded on the five sites above. It does nothing visible until you click the extension icon (or use the keyboard shortcut) and choose to start selecting chats. The only exception is an optional launcher button, which is off by default and which you can turn on in the Options page. Once you start selecting, the extension: looks at the chat list in the site's sidebar and puts a checkbox next to each chat, shows a small panel with your selection and the actions Export, Archive and Delete, when you confirm Delete or Archive, performs the action for the chats you selected. Chat titles and links are held in the page's memory while you are selecting, so the panel can list and count them. They are not saved to disk, are not sent anywhere and are forgotten when you finish selecting or close the page. The extension shows them as plain text and never as HTML. What the extension can access # Data Why Where it goes The chat list in the site's sidebar: each chat's title, link and id To add checkboxes, show your selection, and tell the site which chats to delete or archive Kept in the page's memory only while you are selecting. Not stored. Not transmitted to the author or any third party. The address and tab of the page you are on To know whether the current tab is one of the supported sites, and to start the panel there Used on your device. Not transmitted. Your settings To remember your choices Browser extension storage on your device (see \"What is stored\"). The clipboard (write only) To copy the failure report or the diagnostics when you click the Copy button Written to your clipboard on your click. The extension never reads your clipboard. The extension does not read the messages or the content of any conversation, your account details, your payment details or your cookies. It does not read pages other than the five supported sites. What is stored # The extension stores two small items in storage.local , the browser's local extension storage on your device. It does not use browser sync storage, so the extension itself does not copy this data to your other devices. settings : your choices in the Options page and the panel: interface language, theme, accent color, Fast mode on or off, whether to add checkboxes as you scroll, the extra-confirmation threshold (a number), whether the launcher button is shown, and the position where you last dragged the panel (two numbers). It contains no chat titles, links or account information. supportNudge : the timer for the monthly support reminder (see below): the time of installation, the time the reminder was last shown, how many times it was shown, and whether you chose \"Don't show again\". Versions before 9.0.0 stored the Fast mode choice under a single key named fastApiMode . If it exists, the extension reads it once to carry your choice over to settings . Nothing else is stored. In particular, the extension does not keep a history of your chats, your selections, your deletions, export files or logs. What the extension sends over the network # The extension has no server of its own and makes no requests to its author or to any third party. Its translations and style files are packaged inside it and are read from the extension itself. The only network requests it causes are the following. They happen only after you have selected chats and confirmed Delete or Archive . They are sent from the chat page to the same site, using the session you are already signed in with (the same way the site's own buttons work). They contain no chat titles. The ones that change a chat contain only that chat's id and, for ChatGPT, a short flag saying \"hidden\" or \"archived\": ChatGPT : a request to /api/auth/session to obtain the short-lived access token that the site's own page uses, kept in the page's memory for up to five minutes and never stored; then a PATCH request to /backend-api/conversation/<chat id> to hide (delete) or archive the chat. Claude : a request to /api/organizations to find your organization id, then a DELETE request to /api/organizations/<organization id>/chat_conversations/<chat id> . Claude has no archive in this extension. Grok : a DELETE request to /rest/app-chat/conversations/<chat id> . Grok has no archive in this extension. Gemini : none. Deleting on Gemini is done by clicking through the page's own menu and confirmation dialog, as a person would. These are the sites' own internal endpoints, which are not public or documented, and they can change without notice. This is Fast mode , which is on by default. You can turn it off in the Options page (Behavior) or in the panel's settings. With Fast mode off, or when a request fails, the extension performs the action by clicking through the site's own menus and dialogs instead, one chat at a time, and no extra request is made. The sites' own privacy policies apply to what they do with these requests and with your data. For example, how long ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini or Grok keep a deleted or archived chat is decided by that site, not by the extension. Two more things use the network, but not on the extension's initiative: Links you choose to open. The popup and the Options page contain links to this project's user guide, its GitHub page, the privacy policy, the developer's website (www.enaloo.com), a donation page (Buy Me a Coffee) and the page where you can rate the extension in your browser's store. They open in a new tab only when you click them. Those websites have their own privacy policies. Your browser's update service. Like all store extensions, your browser checks for new versions itself. That is a browser feature, not the extension's. Exporting # Export creates a file from the chats you selected, in JSON, CSV or Markdown format, and your browser saves it to your downloads folder. The file is created on your device and is not uploaded anywhere. It contains each selected chat's title, full link and id, and the site's name and the time of the export. It does not contain any conversation text. Because titles and links can be private, review the file before you share it. Copy report and Copy diagnostics # Copy report (on the result screen after a failed run) puts the titles of the chats that failed and the reason for each on your clipboard, when you click it. It contains chat titles, so look at it before you paste it somewhere public. Copy diagnostics (Options, Privacy) puts the extension version, your browser name and user-agent string, the interface language and your settings on your clipboard, when you click it. It contains no chat titles, links or page content. It is meant for bug reports. Neither is sent anywhere by the extension. Permissions and why each is needed # Permission Why it is needed storage To keep your settings and the support-reminder timer in the browser's local extension storage. activeTab So that when you click the toolbar icon or use the keyboard shortcut, the extension can work with the tab you are on. scripting To load the extension's own scripts into a chat tab that was already open before the extension was installed or updated, so you do not have to reload it. Only the extension's packaged files are injected. Access to the five sites ( chatgpt.com , chat.openai.com , claude.ai , gemini.google.com , grok.com ) Through the extension's content script matches. This is what lets the extension add checkboxes to the chat list and send the delete or archive request on those sites. The browser may describe it as \"Read and change your data on\" those sites. The extension uses it only as described in this policy. In Firefox the same five sites are declared as host permissions and are requested when you install. Keyboard shortcut ( Alt+Shift+B by default) Not a permission. It opens or closes the panel on the supported sites. You can change it in your browser's shortcut settings. The extension does not request access to your browsing history, bookmarks, downloads, cookies, tabs list or any other website. It does not use web_accessible_resources , so sites cannot detect it through its files. Monthly support reminder # AI Bulk Chat Manager is free and has no ads. About two weeks after you install it, and then at most once every 30 days, the extension shows a small heart on its toolbar icon and, when you open the popup, a short note with links to Buy Me a Coffee and to rate the extension. It only ever stores the timer described above, on your device. You can dismiss it with \"Not now\" or turn it off for good with \"Don't show again\". Nothing is sent when it is shown. The links open a third-party website only when you click them. Third parties # There are none. The extension has no analytics, advertising or crash-reporting service, and it loads no remote code, fonts or images. The interface icons are packaged in the extension; they come from the open-source Lucide project (see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md ). The extension is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by OpenAI, Anthropic, Google or xAI. Chrome Web Store Limited Use # The use of information received from browser APIs and the supported sites adheres to the Chrome Web Store User Data Policy , including the Limited Use requirements. Chat titles and links are used only to provide the user-facing features described above, are not transferred to anyone, are not sold, are not used for advertising or to judge creditworthiness, and are not read by humans. Firefox # The Firefox build works the same way and keeps its data in Firefox's local extension storage. Its manifest declares that it collects no data ( data_collection_permissions : none). Removing your data # Settings: Options, Privacy, Reset settings removes the settings item and restores the defaults. Everything: uninstall the extension. The browser then deletes its storage. You can also clear the extension's data from your browser's extension settings. Chats you deleted or archived: these changes were made on the site. The extension cannot undo them. Deleted chats generally cannot be restored; archived ChatGPT chats can be found in ChatGPT's own archive. Export files: files you exported are in your downloads folder. Delete them yourself. The author holds no copy of anything , so there is nothing to request from or delete at the author's end. Children # The extension is not directed at children and collects no personal information from anyone. Open source # The full source code is public at github.com/ehsanenaloo/AI-Bulk-Chat-Manager , under the MIT License, so that every statement above can be checked. Changes to this policy # If the extension's data practices change, this file will be updated in the same release and the change recorded in the changelog . The \"Last updated\" date above will change. Contact # Questions or concerns about privacy: open an issue at github.com/ehsanenaloo/AI-Bulk-Chat-Manager/issues , and do not include personal data. For anything sensitive, use the private reporting process in SECURITY.md ."},{"t":"Troubleshooting and FAQ","u":"guides/troubleshooting-faq.html","d":"Fixes for missing checkboxes, empty chat lists, failed deletes, the popup message Can't reach the site, and answers to common questions.","h":["The panel or the checkboxes do not appear","Select all does not reach every chat","Clicking a chat does not open it","Deleting or archiving did not work","Claude's Recents page","Export problems","Language and look","Frequently asked questions"],"x":"Find the symptom that matches, then try the fix. If nothing helps, see Reporting a problem . Read Limits too: the sites change their pages, and that is the most common cause of trouble. The panel or the checkboxes do not appear # The popup says \"This page isn't supported\" You are not on ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini or Grok. Go to one of them, on its normal address ( chatgpt.com , chat.openai.com , claude.ai , gemini.google.com , grok.com ). Other addresses, including other subdomains, are not supported. The popup says \"Can't reach\" the site The tab was open before the install or an update and could not be attached. Click Reload page , then click the toolbar icon again. In Firefox, check that you allowed access to the chat sites. The shortcut does nothing The shortcut works only on the four supported sites. Check that you are on one. In the Options page, Keyboard shortcut may show Not set because another extension uses the key. Set a different key. See Keyboard and shortcuts . The panel opens but there are no checkboxes The panel says No chats found yet. Open the chat list in the sidebar or scroll it, and they will appear here. Open the sidebar. On a narrow window the site hides it. Scroll the list a little. If the sidebar is open and the list is full of chats but nothing is found, the site may have changed. See Limits . Checkboxes appear only on some chats Turn on Add checkboxes as you scroll and scroll down, or click Load all older chats . I cannot see the panel If you closed it with the X, selecting has ended. Start again from the toolbar icon or the shortcut. If you minimized it, look for its small title bar in the page and click Expand . Options, Privacy, Reset settings puts it back in its default corner. You can also turn on the launcher button in the settings . Select all does not reach every chat # Select all ticks the chats that are in the page right now. The sites load a long history in pages. Click Load all older chats , wait for it to finish, then click Select all . The same goes for Oldest . Clicking a chat does not open it # That is on purpose while you are selecting. A click on a row ticks it. Click Finish selecting (or the X in the panel) to get normal clicking back. Deleting or archiving did not work # Some chats failed Failed chats stay selected, with a reason. Read the reason, then click Retry failed . The table of reasons is in Deleting and archiving . \"The site rejected the session\" You signed out, or the site renewed your session. Reload the page, sign in again and retry. \"The site asked to slow down (rate limit)\" The site limits how fast you can delete. Wait a few minutes and retry with a smaller batch. Everything fails in fast mode The site may have changed its internal requests. Turn Fast mode off (popup, panel settings or Options) and retry. Chats are then handled through the site's menus, which is slower. Please report it . Gemini is slow Gemini always uses its menus, one chat at a time. That is expected. \"Couldn't find the menu item\" and similar menu messages The site's menus changed, or your site language is one the extension cannot read. Retry once. Then report it . The Archive button is missing Archive exists on ChatGPT only. The other sites do not offer archiving. The delete button is disabled Nothing is ticked. Tick a chat. In the confirmation dialog, the red button stays disabled until you tick I understand this can't be undone. when you delete many chats. The chats are back after I reloaded Check the result screen. A chat listed as failed was not deleted. If the result said everything was deleted and a chat still shows, reload once more and report it . Claude's Recents page # Claude has its own Recents page with checkboxes and a delete button built into the site. Those are Claude's, not this extension's. This extension works on the chat list in the sidebar. Use whichever you like. Export problems # Export is disabled Tick at least one chat first. I cannot find the file It is in your browser's download location, named ai-chats-<site>-<date and time>.json (or .csv , .md ). Open your browser's downloads list. Strange characters in Excel Open the CSV through Data, From Text/CSV and choose UTF-8, or use JSON or Markdown. The CSV starts with a marker that most Excel versions use to detect UTF-8. Language and look # The extension shows the wrong language Change it in Options, Appearance, Language . Automatic follows the browser language. The panel does not match my dark mode Set Theme to System , or choose Light or Dark in the Options page. Frequently asked questions # Is it safe to delete hundreds of chats? Review the list in the confirmation dialog. Large deletes need an extra tick. Export first if you may want the titles and links later. Deleting cannot be undone. Can I undo a delete? No. Deleting is the site's own delete. On ChatGPT, Archive is reversible from ChatGPT's settings. Why is Archive only on ChatGPT? The other sites do not offer archiving. Does it read my conversations? No. It reads the chat list that the sidebar shows (titles and links), only while you select, and keeps it only in the page's memory. See Privacy and permissions . Does it send my chats anywhere? No. It has no server. The only requests it causes go to the site you are on, to delete or archive the chats you chose. Does it work on Brave, Opera or Vivaldi? On any Chromium browser that installs Chrome extensions, yes. Firefox needs version 140 or newer. Does it work on a phone? It is built for desktop browsers. Nothing in this guide covers phone browsers. Why checkboxes in the sidebar and a floating panel, not just a popup? Browsers close a popup when you click the page, which made selecting chats clumsy. The panel lives in the page instead. I used version 8. What changed? Version 9 is a rebuild. The selecting tools moved from the popup into the in-page panel, and the extension now also runs on Edge and Firefox. The permissions did not change. The changelog has the details. Is it affiliated with OpenAI, Anthropic, Google or xAI? No. It is an independent project. The names are trademarks of their owners. How do I support it? It is free and has no ads. A rating on the store helps, and so does a coffee: use Support in the popup footer. The developer's website is www.enaloo.com ."},{"t":"Limits and known limitations","u":"guides/limits.html","d":"An honest list of what the extension cannot do: site changes, archive on ChatGPT only, deletes that cannot be undone, and more.","h":["Deleting cannot be undone","The sites change, and then things can break","Where each action works","Archive is for ChatGPT only","Fast mode uses undocumented requests","Very long histories need loading first","The chat list must be visible","Claude's Recents page has its own selection","Tabs open before the install","Firefox","Other limits","Independence"],"x":"This page is the honest list. It is better to know these before a big clean-up than after. Deleting cannot be undone # When the extension deletes a chat, the site deletes it. There is no recycle bin and no undo, in the extension or, in general, on the sites. Archived ChatGPT chats can be restored from ChatGPT. Deleted chats generally cannot. The confirmation dialog, the extra tick for big deletes and Export exist for this reason. Use them. The sites change, and then things can break # This is an independent project. The four sites do not work with it and do not promise to keep their pages the same. It reads each site's page the way you see it, and it uses the same internal requests that the site's own buttons use. The sites do not document those, and they change them without notice. When a site redesigns its sidebar or its menus, one of these can stop working until the extension is updated: checkboxes appear on the wrong things, or not at all; Select all or Load all older chats finds no chats or too few; Delete or Archive fails, with a reason on the result screen; the page-menu route cannot find a button or a menu item. The extension is built to fail safely. If it cannot find the right button, it stops and reports a failure rather than guess. It counts a delete as done only after the chat is really gone from the list. Failed chats stay selected so nothing is lost track of. What was checked for version 9.0.0 The sidebar of Claude was checked against the real site on 2026-10-08. The pages of ChatGPT, Gemini and Grok could not be checked against the real sites for this release. For those three, the code was tested against test copies of the sites, and the approach is carried over from version 8, which real people used. So there is a higher chance that one of them has changed since. If something fails, update the extension, try turning Fast mode off, and report it . Reports are the fastest way to get a site fixed. Where each action works # Site Delete Archive Export Fast mode ChatGPT Yes Yes Yes Yes Claude Yes No Yes Yes Gemini Yes, through its menus No Yes No (always menus) Grok Yes No Yes Yes Archive is for ChatGPT only # The other sites do not offer archiving, so the extension does not either. The button is hidden there. Fast mode uses undocumented requests # Fast mode depends on the sites' internal requests. They can change or be refused. The extension then falls back to the page menus for the chats that failed. The page-menu route is slower, and depends on the site's menus. If both fail, the chat is reported as failed. Very long histories need loading first # The sites load chats a page at a time. The extension can only select what is in the page. For a long history, click Load all older chats before Select all or Oldest . Loading takes longer the more chats you have, and you can stop it at any time. The chat list must be visible # If the sidebar is closed, collapsed or hidden by a small window, the extension sees no chats and the panel says so. Open the sidebar. Chats in collapsed parts of the list are not selected by Select all . Claude's Recents page has its own selection # Claude has a Recents page with checkboxes and a delete button built into the site. They are Claude's own tools. This extension works on the chat list in the sidebar. Tabs open before the install # A chat tab that was open when you installed or updated the extension has no extension in it yet. Click the toolbar icon (or use the shortcut) and the extension attaches itself. If it cannot, reload the tab. See Installation . Firefox # Firefox needs version 140 or newer, on desktop. Firefox asks for access to the five chat sites when you add the extension, and the extension cannot work without it. A temporary add-on is removed when Firefox closes. Other limits # It works only on chatgpt.com , chat.openai.com , claude.ai , gemini.google.com and grok.com . It is built for desktop browsers. The selection exists only in the open page. Reloading the tab loses it. Export is a list of titles and links, not a backup of conversations. It handles chats in the sidebar list. It does not manage projects, folders, shared links or other site features. While a run is going, keep the tab open. Closing it ends the run, and the chats not yet handled stay as they were. Independence # AI Bulk Chat Manager is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by OpenAI, Anthropic, Google or xAI. ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini and Grok are trademarks of their owners."},{"t":"Reporting a problem","u":"guides/reporting-a-problem.html","d":"What to include in a report, what never to paste, how to copy diagnostics, and where the issue forms are.","h":["Before you report","Choose the right form","What to include","Copy diagnostics","What never to paste","What happens next"],"x":"Reports are public on GitHub. Write them so they help the developer without exposing anything private. Before you report # Update the extension to the latest version. Check the version in the popup header. Reload the chat page and try again. If a delete or archive failed, turn Fast mode off and retry. Note whether that changed anything. Look at Troubleshooting and Limits . Choose the right form # All forms are on one page: github.com/ehsanenaloo/AI-Bulk-Chat-Manager/issues/new/choose . You need a free GitHub account. Form Use it when Supported site changed ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini or Grok changed its page and an action stopped working: checkboxes, Select all, Load all older chats, Delete, Archive or Export. Bug report Something else does not work as expected. Question You want to know how to do something. Feature request You have an idea. Describe the problem first. The extension stays local and asks for few permissions, so some ideas will not fit. Translation fix A translation is wrong, awkward or missing. Security problems are different. Do not open a public issue. Use GitHub's private vulnerability report . You can also reach the form from the extension: Options, About, Report a problem . What to include # The site (ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini or Grok) and its address ( chatgpt.com or chat.openai.com ). Your browser , its version and your operating system, for example \"Chrome 150 on Windows 11\". The extension version (the popup header shows it). What you did, what you saw and what you expected. Short steps are best. Which action failed: panel or checkboxes, Select all, Load all older chats, Delete, Archive or Export. The reason text from the result screen, for example Couldn't find the chat's menu button or The site refused the request (404) . Quote the reason. Leave out the chat title. Whether Fast mode was on and whether turning it off changed anything. The diagnostics from the next section. Copy diagnostics # Open the Options page Click the toolbar icon, then the sliders button ( Settings ). Go to Privacy Find the Privacy section. Click Copy diagnostics You see Diagnostics copied. Paste them into a bug report. Paste them into your report. The text looks like this, with your own values: AI Bulk Chat Manager 9.0.0 Browser: chrome (Mozilla/5.0 ...) Interface language: en (setting: auto) Settings: theme=system, accent=teal, fastMode=true, autoLoad=true, confirmThreshold=20, launcher=false No chat titles, addresses or other page content are included in this report. It contains no chat titles, links or page content. Look at it before you paste it anyway. What never to paste # Keep these out of public reports Issues are public. Never paste any of these: chat titles, chat links or conversation text; session cookies, access tokens or API keys; your email address, account details or other personal data; an export file, or the output of Copy report without checking it first. Both contain chat titles. You do not need any of them. If a screenshot helps, crop it so that no chat titles show, or blur them. What happens next # This is a free project kept by one volunteer, so replies are not instant. Reports about a changed site are the most useful, because they point to the exact action that broke. Check the existing issues first, as someone may have reported the same thing. For anything about privacy, read Privacy and permissions . The developer's website is www.enaloo.com ."},{"t":"Overview","u":"index.html","d":"What AI Bulk Chat Manager is, the three-step quick start and the features.","h":[],"x":"Browser extension . User guide Tick many chats. Clear them in one go. AI Bulk Chat Manager puts a checkbox next to every chat in the sidebar of ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini and Grok. Tick what you want gone, then delete, archive or export it all from one small panel. Start in five minutes -> Install it Browse all guides Free and open source (MIT). No account, no server, no analytics. Chrome, Edge and Firefox. [[shot panel | The selection panel next to a chat list with five chats ticked and the Export, Archive and Delete 5 buttons | The panel stays open in the page while you tick chats in the sidebar.]] 4 Supported sites 3 Export formats 11 Interface languages 0 Accounts or servers 01 / Quick start Three steps The whole idea fits in three steps. The quick start walks through them with screenshots. Start selecting Open ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini or Grok. Click the toolbar icon and choose Start selecting chats , or press Alt + Shift + B . Tick your chats Click chats in the sidebar. Use Select all , a title filter, the oldest N, or Shift-click for a range. Export, archive or delete Press Export to save a list first, Archive (ChatGPT only) or Delete . Check the list in the confirmation, then confirm. 02 / Features What it does Built for people with hundreds of old chats and no patience for the three-dot menu. A panel inside the page It stays open while you click in the sidebar and shows a live count. You can drag it, minimize it or close it. Many ways to select Click, Shift-click ranges, Select all, Invert, by title text, the oldest N, and Load all older chats to reach your whole history. You confirm every time A dialog lists exactly what will change and puts focus on Cancel . Big deletes need an extra tick. Fast mode, or by the book Fast mode asks the site directly. If that fails, "}];
